{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457241-relationship-between-prime-and-entropy","id":1457241,"title":"Relationship between Prime and Entropy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-19T17:23:27-07:00","id":1457241,"title":"Relationship between Prime and Entropy","content":"I'm interested in these two Spheres. <br /> <br /> Observations:<br /> <br /> The two Spheres are not opposites, but resemble opposites in some ways.<br /> <br /> Both Spheres deal with Patterns.<br /> <br /> Entropy, alone, cannot create anything.<br /> <br /> Prime can be used to both create or destroy Patterns. Destroying them returns Quintessence to the universe.<br /> <br /> Entropy can alter the probability of a mundane action succeeding.<br /> <br /> Prime deals with and facilitates acquisition of Quintessence, which can be spent to improve the odds of Magick succeeding.<br /> <br /> Both Magick and mundane actions can be used to reduce the difficulty of the other.<br /> <br /> Questions:<br /> <br /> What can a starting character do with 3 ranks in each, rote-wise? <br /> <br /> Higher levels?<br /> <br /> What kind of Paradigm might the character have? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T05:26:22-07:00","id":1457260,"title":"","content":"There's not really a limit on paradigm. Almost every paradigm should include explanations for Prime 3 or Entropy 3 (although you as the player don't need to know the specifics). While I suppose some paradigms lend themselves well to a specialization in one of those two spheres, that is hardly the only reason a starting mage would be that specialized.<br /> <br /> What are you looking for? Inspiration? A better understanding of the two spheres?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-20T14:58:02-07:00","id":1457300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457241-relationship-between-prime-and-entropy?p=1457260#post1457260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you looking for? Inspiration? A better understanding of the two spheres?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of those. It's a starting point for looking at associations between all of the Spheres that are lacking in Sphere entries. I have a way of categorizing the Spheres, by group.<br /> <br /> Group 1) The existing Pattern Spheres + Prime<br /> Group 2) What I call the Dimensional Spheres in which Patterns exist; Spirit, Correspondence, Time.<br /> Group3) Spheres that pertain to being alive, conscious and having an Avatar or potential to have an afterlife; Life, Mind, Spirit. This group links the previous two.<br /> Group 4 - I am considering) Prime and Entropy.<br /> <br /> My diagram keeps getting compressed so that the spacing is misaligned. I will have to get access to a scanner and paste in a picture.<br /> <br /> How do Prime and Entropy fit together, facilitate each other's use or resemble opposites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 08-20-2021, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T03:07:47-07:00","id":1457325,"title":"","content":"Ideas for Entropy 3 and Prime 3.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 lets you make Charms, one use Wonders made in batches. These are covered in Book of Secrets I believe.<br /> <br /> - Lie detection potion, to be consumed before entering an interrogation.<br /> <br /> - Luck potion for minor chance-based events such as how a die, coin or cards fall.<br /> <br /> - A dust which rots, rusts and decays complicated objects.<br /> <br /> - Cursed dolls which can be used to bring bad luck to a person in the mind's eye of the holder, snapping the body of the doll in the process.<br /> <br /> - Luck potion for more complicated things, bringing good fortune outside of games of chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-21T06:41:39-07:00","id":1457331,"title":"","content":"Part of the reason the two spheres have that sometimes-opposite-sometimes-not feeling is that they aren't really working on the same kind of thing. Prime works on the substance of creation: weaving it into patterns*, unweaving it, drawing more quintessence, etc. Entropy does not work on the substance, instead there is an already existing trend of patterns degrading over time and Entropy works on that.<br /> <br /> *with other spheres.<br /> <br /> To use an analogy, let's say you were weaving a tapestry and every night a goblin came out of hiding and started unraveling parts of it. Prime would be the Sphere that governed the fibers and pattern of the tapestry. Entropy would be the Sphere that governed and influenced the goblin. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T22:54:39-07:00","id":1457687,"title":"","content":"Given the chart usually representing the relationship between spheres *<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/8/81/Cycle_of_Effect.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20151222155748\" target=\"_blank\">see here</a>) Entropy plays a role in returning the 'physical' to more of a spiritual/mystical basis (quintessence, which would be the realm of prime.) Prime (and quintessence) move towards the creation of patterns (from mind/idea to spirit.. even inanimate objects can have spirits) whether matter (nonliving), life (living), or forces (stuff that isn't the other two.) And eventually (time and space) mean patterns break down (entropy) which returns them to energy. <br /> <br /> Of course there are always potential for overlaps. Entropy can be more than just physical things - entropy can cover ideas and its tied to the manipulation of time and space (fate and probability) just as prime can cover the 'un-making' of things that overlaps into entropy and the starting stages of 'making' (mind/ideas) - since quintessence can manifest certain kinds of 'mental' energy (psychic powers, pathos of wratihs, conviction of hunters, etc.) you could see Entropy as manipulating (or unmaking) both the physical and the mental (thorugh influence of time and space AND Prime both) <br /> <br /> In a sense a combination of Prime and Entropy might represent something like the Mummy's 'Nomenclature' power (naming or un-naming) - the creation, manipulation or erasure of ideas and/or objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T11:52:02-07:00","id":1457725,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I think the chart <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25533_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25533\" data-vbnamecard=\"25533\">Mister_Dunpeal</a> shows (actually a broken link but I assume it is one of the ones from the core books) shows two important things about Entropy. <br /> <br /> The explicit thing it shows is that Entropy is the recycling sphere that breaks down and returns patterns to more primal forms. <br /> <br /> The implicit thing it shows is that the overall process, from Prime, through concept, location, form and back, goes in one direction. That directionality is also the sphere of Entropy. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T16:56:27-07:00","id":1457738,"title":"","content":"I made a Paint image of it that I can view myself. I know I have come across an explanation of this chart on YouTube. I will try to find it again. It suggests, whether RAW would allow or not, that you could use Entropy to bring a Pattern to an end and draw the Quintessence out as a conjunctional effect using Prime. If you possess the Spheres that govern what happens at both destruction and recreation, you should be able to interrupt the returning of Quintessence to the universe. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T10:11:36-07:00","id":1457800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1457241-relationship-between-prime-and-entropy?p=1457738#post1457738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a Paint image of it that I can view myself. I know I have come across an explanation of this chart on YouTube. I will try to find it again. It suggests, whether RAW would allow or not, that you could use Entropy to bring a Pattern to an end and draw the Quintessence out as a conjunctional effect using Prime. If you possess the Spheres that govern what happens at both destruction and recreation, you should be able to interrupt the returning of Quintessence to the universe. </div> </div> </div> </div>You don\u2019t need entropy for this, it only requires Prime 4. With Prime 4 you can pick up a stone off the ground and strip all the quintessence out of the pattern which utterly destroys the object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 08-27-2021, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}